      "text": "We are given the equation \\(x + y = 4\\) and \\(3xy = 4\\). To solve for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), we start by expressing \\(y\\) in terms of \\(x\\) from the first equation:\n\n\\[y = 4 - x\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(y = 4 - x\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[3x(4 - x) = 4\\]\n\nThis simplifies to a quadratic equation:\n\n\\[12x - 3x^2 = 4\\]\n\\[3x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -12\\), and \\(c = 4\\):\n\n\\[x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^2 - 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4}}{2 \\cdot 3}\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 48}}{6}\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{96}}{6}\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x = \\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\]\n\nWe can rewrite these solutions in the form \\(x = \\frac{a \\pm b\\sqrt{c}}{d}\\). Here, \\(a = 6\\), \\(b = 2\\), \\(c = 6\\), and \\(d = 3\\). Therefore, the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) are 6, 2, 6, and 3, respectively. Adding these values together, we get:\n\n\\[a + b + c + d = 6 + 2 + 6 + 3 = 17\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a + b + c + d\\) is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
