      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the equations:\n\\[ x + y = 4 \\]\n\\[ 3xy = 4 \\]\n\nFirst, we can express \\( y \\) in terms of \\( x \\) from the first equation:\n\\[ y = 4 - x \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 4 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 3x(4 - x) = 4 \\]\n\\[ 12x - 3x^2 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 3x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0 \\]\n\nNow, we solve the quadratic equation \\( 3x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0 \\) using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 3 \\), \\( b = -12 \\), and \\( c = 4 \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{-(-12) \\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^2 - 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4}}{2 \\cdot 3} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 48}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{96}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 2 \\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the solutions for \\( x \\) are:\n\\[ x = 2 + \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 2 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nThese solutions are already in the form \\( x = \\frac{a \\pm b\\sqrt{c}}{d} \\) where \\( a = 6 \\), \\( b = 2 \\), \\( c = 6 \\), and \\( d = 3 \\). Therefore, the values are \\( a = 6 \\), \\( b = 2 \\), \\( c = 6 \\), and \\( d = 3 \\).\n\nThe sum \\( a + b + c + d \\) is:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = 6 + 2 + 6 + 3 = 17 \\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\\[ \\boxed{17} \\]",
